# scenarios/8_credit_note_and_bad_debt.books: loaded by ledger_server into 8_credit_note_and_bad_debt.db the first time it is picked,
# and again by Start over. Amounts are in cents.
title	8. A credit note and a bad debt: revenue that does not come in
about	A credit note takes back part of a sale: customer 1 returns damaged goods, so 500 of the sale is cancelled, the arrow going from Customer 1 back to Sales.
about	A bad debt is a sale that stays revenue but is never paid: customer 2 goes bankrupt, and the 2,000 it owed is written off to Bad debts, a cost. (With VAT, the VAT on it could be claimed back too.)
currency	USD
account	100000	equity	Capital
account	550000	asset	Bank account
account	400001	asset	Customer 1
account	400002	asset	Customer 2
account	700000	revenue	Sales
account	634000	expense	Bad debts
entry	2011-01-02	The founder puts in savings
posting	Capital	-500000
posting	Bank account	500000
entry	2011-02-01	Sale to customer 1: 4,000
posting	Sales	-400000
posting	Customer 1	400000
entry	2011-02-10	Customer 1 returns damaged goods: a credit note of 500
posting	Customer 1	-50000
posting	Sales	50000
entry	2011-03-01	Customer 1 pays the 3,500 it owes
posting	Customer 1	-350000
posting	Bank account	350000
entry	2011-04-01	Sale to customer 2: 2,000
posting	Sales	-200000
posting	Customer 2	200000
entry	2011-10-01	Customer 2 goes bankrupt: its 2,000 is written off
posting	Customer 2	-200000
posting	Bad debts	200000
